From 670e59ce3dbb7e5f13962fcf8e60552a51181ec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomeu Vizoso <tomeu.vizoso@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 11:56:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/37] etnaviv/ml: use a single arena resource instead of
 per-tensor resources

Replace per-tensor pipe_resource allocations with a single arena
(io_rsrc) that all tensors share, matching the approach used in the
ethosu driver. Each tensor now stores just an offset and size within
the arena, tracked via an alloc_id for group management during
concat/split/bypass operations.

This reduces the number of GEM buffer object allocations from one per
tensor to a single allocation for the entire subgraph's feature map
data. The serialization format is updated to version 2 to reflect the
simplified resource management (no resource table needed).
